{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs","id":1241090,"title":"Artifact Costs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-31T17:36:40-07:00","id":1241090,"title":"Artifact Costs","content":"I've been studying the EX3E manual for a few months now and something is still confusing the heck out of me. How are artifacts actually costed out? I haven't been able to find any guidelines in the books for this that is consistent. Is there something I am missing or some reference made by veterans that can give me some insight into how the Artifacts merit actually works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24444-fizzlemeyer","name":"Fizzlemeyer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24444_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T17:52:08-07:00","id":1241093,"title":"","content":"What exactly do you mean? If you mean how artifacts get dots, it depends on what type of item it is and effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T18:39:03-07:00","id":1241103,"title":"","content":"I guess my confusion is that i don't see a cost for a &quot;Basic&quot; artifact weapon or armor, and I cant tell why some of the pre-written ones are costed out the way they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24444-fizzlemeyer","name":"Fizzlemeyer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24444_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T18:43:23-07:00","id":1241104,"title":"","content":"There are no \u201cbasic\u201d Artifact weapons or Armor. Each of them is either a storied piece of antiquity with its own legend or the newly made pinnacle of a Smith\u2019s craft, fully ready to shake the foundations of creation.<br /> <br /> All of them presumably have evocations and all start at 3 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T18:43:49-07:00","id":1241105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fizzlemeyer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1241103#post1241103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my confusion is that i don't see a cost for a &amp;quot;Basic&amp;quot; artifact weapon or armor, and I cant tell why some of the pre-written ones are costed out the way they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this edition, there isn't such a thing. Each artifact starts at 3 and comes with evocations. They go up to 5. 3 are just basic powers while 5 is extremely powerful. Arms of the chosen has a sample set of what the difference between them is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T19:11:24-07:00","id":1241117,"title":"","content":"Artifact 3: increases its wielders capabilities and generally makes them better at what they do <br /> <br /> Artifact 4: unlocks a new playstyle or powers that engage a new method of play (basically anything that grants flight falls in to this category for instance) <br /> <br /> Artifact 5: world shaking wonders of such power that they generally define any scene they are active in. Things like creating vast thunderstorms or calling up volcanoes go here. <br /> <br /> All weapon and armor artifacts fall into one of these categories. Any light, medium, or heavy artifact can hold any different power level. Any of the five magical materials can bring forth powers of any level <br /> <br /> Oh and artifact 3 gets 10 evocations max, Artifact 4 gets 15 at most, and artifact 5 gets no limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T19:54:16-07:00","id":1241129,"title":"","content":"There are Artifact 2 items, but none of them are weapons or armor and they cover the older edition's versions of the utility based 1-2 dot artifacts. Anything combat based is Artifact 3+. <br /> <br /> The listed base stats of the various light/medium/ heavy melee/archery/thrown artifacts and armors are the base stats. This includes Attunement cost of 5 base for all of them i believe. Personalizing them into unique wonders is then the job of the player and/or ST, including adding style and evocation options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T20:41:28-07:00","id":1241143,"title":"","content":"Weapon attunement is a flat 5m. Armor attunement goes from 4m for light armor to 6m for heavy armor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T10:46:41-07:00","id":1241919,"title":"","content":"4 dots is where you tend to get the introduction of new resource statistics like Doom, Intensity, Wakefulness, correct? So the artifact has its own supplemental sub-mechanic like some of the MA styles rather than just working within the existing core mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T02:36:13-07:00","id":1242273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1241919#post1241919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 dots is where you tend to get the introduction of new resource statistics like Doom, Intensity, Wakefulness, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there are 3-dot Artifacts like that. Doom is actually attached to one of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T03:42:49-07:00","id":1242285,"title":"","content":"The main rule is that evocations show up at artifact 3 and up. So if you did theoretically make a daiklave with no evocations, it would be two dots.<br /> <br /> You're not supposed to do that, but go nuts. It's not like we have squads of canon-enforcing ninjas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T05:38:31-07:00","id":1242312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242285#post1242285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not supposed to do that, but go nuts. It's not like we have squads of canon-enforcing ninjas.</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>Bloodthirsty Canon</b></i>, a starmetal and soulsteel infinite chakram, was made by Chejop Kejack in the aftermath of the Usurpation. Those scarred by its Old Realm-inscribed edges forever earn the enmity of an obscure spirit known as the <i>Canon Ninja</i>, who obsess over the state of cryptic trivia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-03-2018, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T06:28:29-07:00","id":1242334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242285#post1242285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main rule is that evocations show up at artifact 3 and up. So if you did theoretically make a daiklave with no evocations, it would be two dots.<br /> <br /> You're not supposed to do that, but go nuts. It's not like we have squads of canon-enforcing ninjas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd generally argue against it since when a person buys a daiklave with no free Evocations, they still have to invest xp into it to get htem, while the guy who just got a hypothetical two-dot one with no Evocations in effect gets a point for free. Making Evocatiosn require 3 and Artifacts require it I think is there in part so that if you want the stats, you have to pony-up.<br /> <br /> That said, Artifact 2 might get you a mortal statted weapon with some unique supernatural things, but an actual daiklave I'd advise gainst, even if it is ultimatley one's own game on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T07:25:46-07:00","id":1242347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242334#post1242334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd generally argue against it since when a person buys a daiklave with no free Evocations, they still have to invest xp into it to get htem, while the guy who just got a hypothetical two-dot one with no Evocations in effect gets a point for free. Making Evocatiosn require 3 and Artifacts require it I think is there in part so that if you want the stats, you have to pony-up.<br /> <br /> That said, Artifact 2 might get you a mortal statted weapon with some unique supernatural things, but an actual daiklave I'd advise gainst, even if it is ultimatley one's own game on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artifacts found in core and Arms aren't just weapons/armors with better statlines even before you start purchasing Evocations. Gorgon can still wake even if you haven't bought a single Evocation for it yet, and will add its Wakefulness rating to Withering damage. Adorei gives you +1 Accuracy right off the bat. Spring Razor gives you its first Evocation for free. So on and so forth.<br /> <br /> In light of this, one could argue a hypothetical 2-dot weapon/armor with just the base artifact statline, no immediate bonus and no Evocations to buy, would be priced fairly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T07:39:09-07:00","id":1242351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242285#post1242285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main rule is that evocations show up at artifact 3 and up. So if you did theoretically make a daiklave with no evocations, it would be two dots.</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>A Really Nice Daiklave</b></i> ( ** ) - This is a really nice Daiklave. It is sturdily built and, even if the design is very orthodox, it fits nicely in the hand. It comes with a matching scabbard, and the whole set is decorated in a way that's actually really nice, if you give it much notice. A Really Nice Daiklave is part of a panoply forged by a group of artisans known as the Conclave of the Magnificent Spark. This sect's guiding tenet is that the excellence and might of the Chosen should not be obscured by mere objects. Those who carry A Really Nice Daiklave can be sure that their weapon will not fail them in combat, nor will it outshine their own glory. It is also really nicely weighted and pleasant to swing.<br /> <br /> Evocations - Probably none. Chosen who bear A Really Nice Daiklave and have a positive Intimacy toward displaying their own prowess may gain 1 Willpower when they defeat a significant foe without the use of Evocations from any source. Whether this effect is itself an Evocation is mildly debated, occasionally; whether it is or is not, the effect has no XP cost and is discovered the first time the conditions are met.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T08:00:32-07:00","id":1242358,"title":"","content":"Guys, the first line in Arms of the Chosen under 'Designing Artifacts and Evocations' states:<br /> &quot;<b>Every </b>artifact armor or weapon, and many a unique wonder rated at 3+ dots, has Evocations [...]&quot;<br /> <br /> Bolding mine. So by this metric, you can't do an artifact 2 weapon. You can do an artifact 2 lesser wonder, but it won't have evocations, basically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T08:05:42-07:00","id":1242359,"title":"","content":"*swimming further from canon*<br /> <br /> yes, we know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T08:26:53-07:00","id":1242362,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d like to point out that on 593-594 in the core book, it says all the weapons listed there (meaning Every artifact weapon type in the book) is a minimum 3 dots. It\u2019s not just that evocations unlock at 3 dots and above, it\u2019s that only artifact 3 or above is what are for artifact weapons. This is again I believe a design intent to prevent mass production of artifact weapons, a major problem in second edition, as well as making artifact weapons not feel interchangeable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T08:33:18-07:00","id":1242366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242359#post1242359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*swimming further from canon*<br /> <br /> yes, we know.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may, but your original post framed it as if it was perfectly reasonable to just make artifact weapons at 2 dots. Except RAW it isn't.<br /> <br /> OP doesn't own Arms, best not to assume everyone knows that you're talking pure orichalcum rule here.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, I don't know for sure OP doesn't own arms, but the fact remains that this entire thread was asking for clarification on RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 08-03-2018, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T09:10:01-07:00","id":1242384,"title":"","content":"See, I figured I made that clear when I spoke of the canon-enforcing ninjas, but ok.<br /> <br /> To summarise: The artifact cost of weapons is almost entirely a feature of their evocations. Without them, there's no real difference between a three dot and a five dot daiklave. All artifact weapons are assumed to have evocations, and only artifacts of three dots and above can have evocations.<br /> <br /> For these two reasons, by raw, there is no such thing as a two-dot artifact weapon.<br /> <br /> And just to be clear, in 3e there's no such thing as a one-dot artifact, period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T10:54:18-07:00","id":1242425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242384#post1242384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I figured I made that clear when I spoke of the canon-enforcing ninjas, but ok.<br /> <br /> To summarise: The artifact cost of weapons is almost entirely a feature of their evocations. Without them, there's no real difference between a three dot and a five dot daiklave. All artifact weapons are assumed to have evocations, and only artifacts of three dots and above can have evocations.<br /> <br /> For these two reasons, by raw, there is no such thing as a two-dot artifact weapon.<br /> <br /> And just to be clear, in 3e there's no such thing as a one-dot artifact, period.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree that this is about canon enforcement, so much as that this is trying to explain knock on effects and why these things were changed. The knowing why a thing was changed, and the intent with that change, mean a lot of you are trying to alter the setting because you run into secondary effects you may not intend.<br /> <br /> For instance, the reasoning I derive from both CORE and Arms stems from a dev desire to remove mass produced/industrialized artifact creation from happening, which is part of the overall strategy to make artifacts and sorcery in the 1st age to have been \u201cmodern day tech but with different power sources\u201d that 2e was notorious for.<br /> <br /> Adding back in 2 dot artifacts begins to undo this, as does doing things like making it easy for mortals to attune to said artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T13:40:20-07:00","id":1242477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242425#post1242425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree that this is about canon enforcement, so much as that this is trying to explain knock on effects and why these things were changed. The knowing why a thing was changed, and the intent with that change, mean a lot of you are trying to alter the setting because you run into secondary effects you may not intend.<br /> <br /> For instance, the reasoning I derive from both CORE and Arms stems from a dev desire to remove mass produced/industrialized artifact creation from happening, which is part of the overall strategy to make artifacts and sorcery in the 1st age to have been \u201cmodern day tech but with different power sources\u201d that 2e was notorious for.<br /> <br /> Adding back in 2 dot artifacts begins to undo this, as does doing things like making it easy for mortals to attune to said artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>A solar who wants to churn out a bunch of diaklaves can pretty easily with their own charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T14:04:19-07:00","id":1242484,"title":"","content":"Ehh, if you try and churn them out you'll run out of Gold XP, unless you have the entire 11-charm xp-generating tree, several craft abilities at 5, and a good essence score.<br /> <br /> I do have all of those, but making 3 artefacts in a story still used up all my gold xp (for a few sessions, then I'll probably be able to make more; but having downtime without a bunch of adventuring sessions wouldn't be much use).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-03-2018, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T14:27:55-07:00","id":1242488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242477#post1242477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A solar who wants to churn out a bunch of diaklaves can pretty easily with their own charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between one solar churning out 100 daiklaves and 100 Dragonblooded being able to churn out 1000 daiklaves each.<br /> <br /> Edit: yes I am being hyperbolic for effect, but it\u2019s a matter of scale is what I am saying and illustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","user":"Saipjas","date":". 08-03-2018, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T14:36:12-07:00","id":1242493,"title":"","content":"Luckily, not every Chosen do the whole crafting thing. Otherwise they'd all also have to invest a whole lot in bureaucracy. Exotic materials are hard to get by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amateur drawsmith","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2847-thatsmellygoblin","name":"ThatSmellyGoblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2847_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T14:46:45-07:00","id":1242501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatSmellyGoblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242493#post1242493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luckily, not every Chosen do the whole crafting thing. Otherwise they'd all also have to invest a whole lot in bureaucracy. Exotic materials are hard to get by.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are operating at the level of an individual absolutely, if you are leading a Creation spanning imperial polity and can effectively create a societal structure that can industrialize, it becomes much more problematic. Hence the efforts by the Devs to ensure that the ability to industrialize artifacts is NOT a thing mechanically in addition to placing societal barriers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T16:25:56-07:00","id":1242525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242501#post1242501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you are operating at the level of an individual absolutely, if you are leading a Creation spanning imperial polity and can effectively create a societal structure that can industrialize, it becomes much more problematic. Hence the efforts by the Devs to ensure that the ability to industrialize artifacts is NOT a thing mechanically in addition to placing societal barriers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too bad the old devs really didn't do a good job at it. Rather than create a charmset that would cultivate wonders, solars are expected to churn them out to gain White xp. It's a really good system for incentivizing industrialization. But that's probably the least of the solar craft tree's issues.<br /> <br /> Also, a solar crafter, can just get enough god-blooded, ( or his own children with high essence) equip and train them, and then conquer places to get more materials. Bureaucracy isn't the only way to get materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 08-03-2018, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T17:08:55-07:00","id":1242532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242477#post1242477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A solar who wants to churn out a bunch of diaklaves can pretty easily with their own charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me their stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T17:19:18-07:00","id":1242537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242532#post1242532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tell me their stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stories are started after they're created. They aren't created with one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T17:22:13-07:00","id":1242539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242525#post1242525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Too bad the old devs really didn't do a good job at it. Rather than create a charmset that would cultivate wonders, solars are expected to churn them out to gain White xp. It's a really good system for incentivizing industrialization. But that's probably the least of the solar craft tree's issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>While there are a number of things I dislike about the Solar craft charmset, and wish I could un-buy all those Craft charms I've got for my Zenith, one good thing I will say about it is that I don't think it encourages industrialisation. Or rather, it'd be good for you if you could, but the charmset doesn't really let you. It's too reliant on points generated by sessions of active play to allow you to just build a factory and spend a bunch of downtime doing stuff there. At least, in my experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, a solar crafter, can just get enough god-blooded, ( or his own children with high essence) equip and train them, and then conquer places to get more materials. Bureaucracy isn't the only way to get materials. </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's that many god-blooded who can channel essence waiting around to be recruited to conquer places. I'd think it'd be easier to recruit, well, a regular army.<br /> But that's not necessarily something a Crafter is good at (equipping an army though...).<br /> <br /> I'd think your best bet is to ally with a Dawn with an army, rather than try recruiting your own, and have your Dawn buddy conquer places and give you the magical materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T17:37:23-07:00","id":1242544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242539#post1242539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While there are a number of things I dislike about the Solar craft charmset, and wish I could un-buy all those Craft charms I've got for my Zenith, one good thing I will say about it is that I don't think it encourages industrialisation. Or rather, it'd be good for you if you could, but the charmset doesn't really let you. It's too reliant on points generated by sessions of active play to allow you to just build a factory and spend a bunch of downtime doing stuff there. At least, in my experience.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>When I mean industrialization, I mean it just takes a solar to act as a factory. Granted there are a lot of things he could be doing instead but doesn't really change the fact that the charmset just incentives creating mundane goods and artifacts over say building blue prints, refining designs and techniques, or other methods that would naturally take place in creating things. Instead you're just expected to create them instead of working towards it. I will say, 2e had a lot of flaws but I will say having to make an artifact to make a bigger artifact was always a good idea in my opinion. A component that's relatively useless but necessary to make something else, just shows how much work goes into it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T17:47:01-07:00","id":1242549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242537#post1242537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The stories are started after they're created. They aren't created with one.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Beloved Adorei was created for no reason at all?<br /> <br /> By the way, the white points you feel so incentivized to get; what do you plan for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T18:16:50-07:00","id":1242556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242549#post1242549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Beloved Adorei was created for no reason at all?<br /> <br /> By the way, the white points you feel so incentivized to get; what do you plan for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were created for a reason but they didn't have a story till quite a while after their creation. Also, it still doesn't stop a solar from just churning ut diaklaives unless your going to just veto his perfectly valid tactic. My point is, the design of the craft charms doesn't follow with the design principles set up in place. Also the white points in this case would probably be put towards a warstrider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T18:28:47-07:00","id":1242559,"title":"","content":"If it was &quot;perfectly valid,&quot; it wouldn't need a veto.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-03-2018, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T19:05:20-07:00","id":1242574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242484#post1242484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehh, if you try and churn them out you'll run out of Gold XP, unless you have the entire 11-charm xp-generating tree, several craft abilities at 5, and a good essence score.</div> </div> </div> </div>By my calculations a solar with just six power charms (Divine Inspiration Technique and its prerequisites) will on average get more gold points than they spend per daiklave made. (This is assuming craft (blacksmithing) 5 (swords +1), craft (artifacts) 5 (daiklaves +1), str 5, int 5, exceptional tools, a forge in which they can safely build their anima up to burning without attracting the wyld hunt and the ability to achieve at least one one-point stunt per daiklave.)<br /> <br /> If you want to make arbitrarily many at once and not do any stunts on the completion rolls, you also need Sublime Transference, making a total of eight craft charms. You'll still run into craft point limitations at the beginning (since you pay for the craft slots up front and don't get the rewards until you complete the projects, and also I'm including the 5gp/artifact reward that you don't get until the end of the story), but no matter what rate you want to produce daiklaves at you'll eventually reach a point where you can produce daiklaves at that rate without using up craft points. (You still need to meet basic objectives with the daiklaves you make to get the rewards, but if it *doesn't* meet any basic objectives, why are you even making daiklaves?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","user":"rj.au","date":".  added second paragraph 08-03-2018, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T19:17:42-07:00","id":1242575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242559#post1242559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it was &amp;quot;perfectly valid,&amp;quot; it wouldn't need a veto.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's literally nothing in the entire core book that stops it from happening, except a dev intention to keep artifacts as &quot;wonders&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T20:04:53-07:00","id":1242583,"title":"","content":"for me it'd be coming up with all the different names and evocations of the weapons. That sounds like hell to be quite honest.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your name is uh....&quot; rapid looking around. &quot;Forge...hand....Tongs... ForgeHandTongs.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T21:16:39-07:00","id":1242601,"title":"","content":"I think the idea in 3e is the Solar who is making a buncha swords is like some legendary swordsmith probably known for making a lot of badass magical swords. The anime and light novel series <b>Katanagatari</b> seems to be pretty much what I imagine a lot of Solar swordsmith work looks like. Maybe a bit more prolific, but if it's getting toth eh point you're equipping armies I think it's just going a bit into pushing the letter of the rules over the spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T02:10:42-07:00","id":1242662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rj.au</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242574#post1242574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By my calculations a solar with just six power charms (Divine Inspiration Technique and its prerequisites) will on average get more gold points than they spend per daiklave made. (This is assuming craft (blacksmithing) 5 (swords +1), craft (artifacts) 5 (daiklaves +1), str 5, int 5, exceptional tools, a forge in which they can safely build their anima up to burning without attracting the wyld hunt and the ability to achieve at least one one-point stunt per daiklave.)<br /> <br /> If you want to make arbitrarily many at once and not do any stunts on the completion rolls, you also need Sublime Transference, making a total of eight craft charms. You'll still run into craft point limitations at the beginning (since you pay for the craft slots up front and don't get the rewards until you complete the projects, and also I'm including the 5gp/artifact reward that you don't get until the end of the story), but no matter what rate you want to produce daiklaves at you'll eventually reach a point where you can produce daiklaves at that rate without using up craft points. (You still need to meet basic objectives with the daiklaves you make to get the rewards, but if it *doesn't* meet any basic objectives, why are you even making daiklaves?)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's.... actually a good point, I went and checked and I think you're right about how you can produce plenty of gold points if you just roll amazingly enough. I never really thought before about the rewards from making it, because I didn't get that much from the artefacts I made, due to not having all those power charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T02:35:03-07:00","id":1242666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242556#post1242556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were created for a reason but they didn't have a story till quite a while after their creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand your read on the creation story of that Artifact.<br /> <br /> And it goes for the majority of Artifacts that we've had written across three books; that their Evocation suites are a synthesis of the intention and circumstances of their creation and the story of what they were then used for. V'neef's powerbow has the power to summon a giant magic wolf as a familiar because taming it is a thing that she did with it, but she was able to tame a giant magic wolf with a powerbow because the thing was commissioned for her to be a companion to go with her tendency to wander off alone into the wilderness.<br /> <br /> Or what about the daiklave made from the remains of the sword of a Cathak woman who sacrificed herself, whose Evocations revolve entirely around themes of self-sacrifice and defence of comrades in arms; that one seems to owe basically everything that it is to its origin story. Or House Iselsi's vengeance tiger claws.<br /> <br /> None of these are blank slates. I can think of maybe two Artifacts out of the several dozen written by now in which we're not given insight into their origins (and of those, one is because its origin is relatively mysterious).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it still doesn't stop a solar from just churning ut diaklaives unless your going to just veto his perfectly valid tactic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, absolutely. There should absolutely be a veto on making a daiklave if the player has no thought or intention behind what its character is going to be, and is making it perfunctorily. Not least because the rules make a point of how, if your crafting ends in failure, what you had in mind for the daiklave can never exist at all; there needs to be something there to be checked off.<br /> <br /> Heck, there's something more to engage with in the point if it was referring to Artifacts that aren't actually required to be unique; we can talk about the problem with milling white craft points out of over-production of belts of shadow walking or something.<br /> <br /> But you chose daiklaves, which suggests to me a very curious read of all of the daiklaves that we've been given.<br /> <br /> Heck, Flying Silver Dream has a story coming out of its creation <i>that is a continuation</i> of the story out of the creation of Courante and Guillard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the white points in this case would probably be put towards a warstrider.</div> </div> </div> </div>A warstrider that I presume isn't going to take any cues from the idea of one that has powers coming out of it having been made as a romantic gesture from one Solar to another.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T03:04:43-07:00","id":1242671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242537#post1242537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The stories are started after they're created. They aren't created with one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's... literally not how any of the artifact weapons in Arms of the Chosen are presented.<ul><li>Sunflash was forged to attract the attention of a god.</li> <li>Strife's Crucible was created by a Sidereal to test other Exalted after the Usurpation.</li> <li>Rainwalker was made from the stolen grace of a Fair Folk after a Lunar engaged in 70 days of diplomacy</li> <li>Courante and Galliard were made to celebrate the trust and love of two companions.</li> </ul>I don't often tell people they're Doing It Wrong but anyone who thinks Exalted is encouraging &quot;industrialization&quot; of artifacts is Doing It Wrong. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T18:15:07-07:00","id":1242834,"title":"","content":"Within reason I'd let someone create a batch of daiklaves with a shared origin story. i.e. 5 being made in memory of a hearth who sacrificed their lives to stop some great evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T10:07:16-07:00","id":1242973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242834#post1242834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within reason I'd let someone create a batch of daiklaves with a shared origin story. i.e. 5 being made in memory of a hearth who sacrificed their lives to stop some great evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the Five Voltron Lions.<br /> <br /> In a different fashion, how the Brass Legion was possible, or the entire network of the Gates of Passage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T17:18:05-07:00","id":1243986,"title":"","content":"3e's obnoxious &quot;get rid of everything that made 2e cool and spit on it&quot; attitude is honestly one of its worst traits. Sometimes I just want a goddamn black jade tetsubou without all this evocation busywork and there is literally nothing wrong with mass producing artifacts (&quot;Factory-Cathedrals were cool as hell&quot; is a hill I will die on forever). If my solar has a block of jade I should be able to pump out a sword in a few days, sheesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T17:22:42-07:00","id":1243987,"title":"","content":"I think you're projecting, here. 3E has never directly shat on 2E; that's mostly been the fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T18:05:13-07:00","id":1243997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rj.au</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242574#post1242574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(You still need to meet basic objectives with the daiklaves you make to get the rewards, but if it *doesn't* meet any basic objectives, why are you even making daiklaves?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you\u2019re thinking with crafting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T18:56:46-07:00","id":1244011,"title":"","content":"I would also suggest that while an artifact may be storied, there's no requirement for a character to learn those Evocations. If you don't want your character using Evocations but you want an artifact weapon, just take a 3 dot artifact weapon and don't learn any Evocations.<br /> <br /> The worst case Scenario is, what, you decide you actually like the idea of getting charms from being connected to your weapon and write a couple up?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T23:38:47-07:00","id":1244061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1243987#post1243987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're projecting, here. 3E has never directly shat on 2E; that's mostly been the fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>A huge amount of 3e's design philsophy was fixing what the devs thought was wrong with 2e. That's blatantly obvious from pre-release interviews/questions and the like.<br /> <br /> And like, I'm not saying that 2e is perfect. It was a clustershitfuck with some absolutely ATROCIOUS segments such as the entire combat system <i>not working</i>, mind-control charms, literally everything about Infernals besides their amazing basic concept and charms, SMA being broken as shit, DB's being mechanically worthless, and the like. But at the same time, there are some really annoying decisions I feel have been made in an effort to fix stuff I don't think really need fixing, such as 3e going out of its way to actively reject the Science Fantasy trappings of the First Age in 2e. Another example would be Infernals no longer using Yozi charms because one person happened to game the system to change the Yozi's natures and apparently this was such a massive sin that the coolest thing about Infernals had to die in a fire instead of just saying &quot;no you can't irreversibly change the Yozi's through altering their charm trees&quot;. But I digress.<br /> <br /> If I want my Solar to be able to make Daiklaves practically in her sleep like a human assembly line, then assuming I have a crapload of MM and the proper equipment, there should be no reason why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 08-09-2018, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T01:11:04-07:00","id":1244075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1242358#post1242358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, the first line in Arms of the Chosen under 'Designing Artifacts and Evocations' states:<br /> &quot;<b>Every </b>artifact armor or weapon, and many a unique wonder rated at 3+ dots, has Evocations [...]&quot;<br /> <br /> Bolding mine. So by this metric, you can't do an artifact 2 weapon. You can do an artifact 2 lesser wonder, but it won't have evocations, basically.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could also possibly be read to mean that every 3+ artifact armor and weapons, as well as some 3+ non-armor non-weapon artifacts have evocations, without saying anything about (non)existence of 1-2 dot ones (beyond the fact that even if they do exist, they would not have evocations).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T01:41:18-07:00","id":1244080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1243986#post1243986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I just want a goddamn black jade tetsubou without all this evocation busywork</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing obligating a player to buy up their Artifact's whole Evocation cascade.<br /> <br /> And most of the published Artifacts are generous enough to give somebody a starter power for free, to get a bit of extra bang for their buck. Stormcaller still lets you do something that feels like a powerful mystical weapon without needing to spend any XP on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">there is literally nothing wrong with mass producing artifacts</div> </div> </div> </div>So what does that say about all of the people that see something wrong with that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my solar has a block of jade I should be able to pump out a sword in a few days, sheesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that even possible in Second Edition?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T03:24:00-07:00","id":1244089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1244080#post1244080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was that even possible in Second Edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depressingly possible. One of the players in my first 2e game had cobbled together a monstrosity that could -at chargen- craft a daiklave inside of a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T03:30:24-07:00","id":1244090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1244061#post1244061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A huge amount of 3e's design philsophy was fixing what the devs thought was wrong with 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how you do any edition that's not the same product as before with a higher number on the cover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1243986#post1243986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e's obnoxious &quot;get rid of everything that made 2e cool and spit on it&quot; attitude is honestly one of its worst traits.</div> </div> </div> </div> and a lot of 2e fans are constantly tilting at windmills like they're looking for battles in their personal edition war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":1115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","user":"The Hug Ninja","date":". 08-09-2018, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T07:47:26-07:00","id":1244140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1244075#post1244075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could also possibly be read to mean that every 3+ artifact armor and weapons, as well as some 3+ non-armor non-weapon artifacts have evocations, without saying anything about (non)existence of 1-2 dot ones (beyond the fact that even if they do exist, they would not have evocations).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the lines in the core that all artifact armor and weapons listed there are at minimum artifact 3. So theoretically you <i>could</i> have an artifact 2 weapon but it would have to be a separate category of weapon from anything we've got stats for so far.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It's also explicit there that all artifact weapons and armor have evocations. If you were to rewrite that sentence into two they would be: &quot;Every artifact armor or weapon has Evocations that depict its unique legacy and power. Many a unique wonder rated at 3+ dots has evocations that depict its unique legacy and power.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 08-09-2018, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T10:09:08-07:00","id":1244187,"title":"","content":"It took me a week in 3e to make 2 short daiklaives. That doesn't really seem very onerous. (Though the XP necessary was!)<br /> <br /> Tbh, I don't see any value in churning out daiklaives. What are you going to do with them? Between our 6 PCs we've already got 8 artefact weapons (plus some spares they looted from the Wyld Hunt years ago and I'm sure have forgotten about), 2 sets of artefact plate, and a warstrider. Making another 10 daiklaives just devalues them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T11:22:50-07:00","id":1244214,"title":"","content":"Also you totally can make a jade sword in a day as a Solar.<br /> <br /> It will be a mundane sword made of jade, with no artifact evocations, excessive weight, and mundane stats.<br /> <br /> But you can totally perform a project to make a jade sword in a day.<br /> <br /> Imbuing that sword with adequate essence and fostering a spirit of the blade itself to produce wondrous powers? That takes time. Time on par with &quot;Building an entire palace complex&quot;. Three months, without charms.<br /> <br /> &quot;But I can just make a palace complex in a day with CNNT--&quot; No, you can't. Craftsman Needs No Tools is limited to Basic/Major projects. A palace complex is a Superior project. That takes Thousand Forge Hands, WHICH notably does not allow a palace complex in a day; it makes it take (6-Essence) weeks, the same as a 3-dot daiklave, instead of &quot;3 months&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T13:51:25-07:00","id":1244264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1244187#post1244187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It took me a week in 3e to make 2 short daiklaives. That doesn't really seem very onerous. (Though the XP necessary was!)<br /> <br /> Tbh, I don't see any value in churning out daiklaives. What are you going to do with them? Between our 6 PCs we've already got 8 artefact weapons (plus some spares they looted from the Wyld Hunt years ago and I'm sure have forgotten about), 2 sets of artefact plate, and a warstrider. Making another 10 daiklaives just devalues them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less about churning out daiklaves and more about 3e's insistence that you can't mass-produce artifacts in any shape or way whatsoever because god forbid the fucking god kings of the earth exalt the living conditions of their subjects when they finally manage to take over the realm again! Nah only Solars get cool shit, everyone else can just be a farmer outside of the shining golden manse using the same tools they did when they were farmers suffering under the realm's taxes apparently. Want your Twilight to create a glorious shining magitech city based on motonic science and the wrangling of the supernatural into codified artifice? Only LAME-O's wanna do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T14:29:10-07:00","id":1244273,"title":"","content":"Honestly, that's not about mass production. A magitech city can probably just be done as a giant N/A artefact (a guy in our game spent a year of downtime making a giant magic city). The issue there is the de-emphasis of the magitech aesthetic. Which is something they have done, and one different people have different opinions about, and I'm not saying you're wrong about that (my own opinion is mixed), but it's not about mass production, in terms of the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-09-2018, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T15:45:01-07:00","id":1244298,"title":"","content":"Or sorcerous workings, or standard projects [as in the project system of which crafting the desired wonders you want would probably be a component]. There's ways, it's just not so simple as 2e's &quot;I hide in my workshop for a little while and shit out a utopia&quot;.<br /> <br /> With ST permission, you could totally have a manse that serves as a factory-cathedral! You'd have to define what this august factory-cathedral does in 3e, possibly investing in evocations to enhance it, but just because the setting book isn't jerking itself stupid over how these manses are the biggest baddest things ever that only Solars could make doesn't mean &quot;a place of power that has been dedicated to the production of wonders&quot; is suddenly outlawed.<br /> <br /> Capital A Artifacts in 3e are pretty much useless for mortal personal use anyway; they require attunement, which is an ability you can't just punch into a mortal anymore, their power typically lies in evocations rather than just getting a free suite of always-on boosts,.. If you want to improve the lives of mortals, what you need is wondrous excellent infrastructure and sorcerous boons, not dumping a Glorious Golden iPad into their hands.<br /> <br /> edit: I mean I personally think &quot;motonic science&quot; is lame buzzwords trying to make magic sound KEWLer by being all 'sciencesque', but as Levi notes below, Arms doesn't shit on it, it just doesn't mention it. Arms aims to make magic cooler by making magic cool and exciting for being magic rather than make it not-magic.<br /> <b>Improving the lives of your subjects</b>: Giving them a Glorious Golden Hoe won't do shit because they can't use it, by definition of being Mortal. You could create an automaton to assist with the harvest as per a Brass Legionnaire, perhaps. Or use sorcerous workings to breed hardy, prolifically fruiting crops that are easier to harvest. Or use your great solar talent to organize social welfare systems to support all members of society. But just snapping your fingers and &quot;i crafted a utopia&quot;, nah. That's lame. 3e tells you to be creative instead of just saying &quot;30 successes on Craft: Utopia, what'd I get?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 08-09-2018, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T15:51:41-07:00","id":1244302,"title":"","content":"Frostav, Arms of the Chosen did not depict things that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T01:33:18-07:00","id":1244415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1244214#post1244214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also you totally can make a jade sword in a day as a Solar.<br /> <br /> It will be a mundane sword made of jade, with no artifact evocations, excessive weight, and mundane stats..</div> </div> </div> </div>Jade actually weighs less than steel (two fifths as much at the heaviest, according to my brief internet research), so it wouldn't be excessively heavy unless you made it daiklave-sized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T01:40:51-07:00","id":1244417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rj.au</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1244415#post1244415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jade actually weighs less than steel (two fifths as much at the heaviest, according to my brief internet research)</div> </div> </div> </div>The mystical five colour jade is not the same substance as the mundane nephrite. That doesn't necessarily make your point incorrect, but the underlying reasoning would be flawed.<br /> <br /> If one wanted to determine the density of the magical material jade, it could probably be done by comparing the figures given for a talent of the stuff; I believe that prior Editions gave them with more precision.<br /> <br /> That being said, I believe that you're correct in how an object of regular size made from jade or any other magical material would not be particularly heavy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T01:49:47-07:00","id":1244419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1244187#post1244187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It took me a week in 3e to make 2 short daiklaives. That doesn't really seem very onerous. (Though the XP necessary was!)<br /> <br /> Tbh, I don't see any value in churning out daiklaives. What are you going to do with them? Between our 6 PCs we've already got 8 artefact weapons (plus some spares they looted from the Wyld Hunt years ago and I'm sure have forgotten about), 2 sets of artefact plate, and a warstrider. Making another 10 daiklaives just devalues them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give them to martially inclined gods to win their favour. Supply them to outcaste terrestrial families to incentivise them to stay on your good side. Give them to NPC celestial exalted in exchange for their help. Give them to desperate dynasts willing to bargain with anathemas in the hope of defeating their rivals. Give them to abyssals in exchange for eclipse-sanctified vows not to attack your subjects. Use a different one each story then sell them to collectors of historically important weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T06:59:44-07:00","id":1244473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1244264#post1244264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's less about churning out daiklaves and more about 3e's insistence that you can't mass-produce artifacts in any shape or way whatsoever because god forbid the fucking god kings of the earth exalt the living conditions of their subjects when they finally manage to take over the realm again! Nah only Solars get cool shit, everyone else can just be a farmer outside of the shining golden manse using the same tools they did when they were farmers suffering under the realm's taxes apparently. Want your Twilight to create a glorious shining magitech city based on motonic science and the wrangling of the supernatural into codified artifice? Only LAME-O's wanna do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, to respond to this in more detail:<br /> <br /> Right off the bat, the corebook contains First Age Artifice, with rules for acquiring the crafting skill and making the stuff, and guidelines about what the stuff is. That's more than any prior core book gave in terms of making those kinds of things, and makes them a bit foundational to the setting. They're not strictly technological in aesthetic, but neither do they exclude such things, so they exist as something to strive for.<br /> <br /> It is difficult, mind; there are a few hoops one has to jump through in order to build up the Ability for it, and I'd say the big obstacle is the dependence on sorcerous workings. Even with the best possible combination of Craft Charms, that's probably going to be the big one; the additional time and difficulty put on depending on how far you have developed your sorcery (the one thing that Solars get no shortcuts on), as well as the costs in xp. It's possible to make things that are individually unusual in the genre of the setting, but doing it on a scale that might transform the setting overall is probably something to explore over much of the length of a chronicle.<br /> <br /> Still, in addition to that, Arms of the Chosen puts forward a point that the First Age possessed miraculous infrastructure for the creation of things such as Brass Legionnaires in batches, or as a repeat process of a standard model, so the capacity for that also exists in the setting.<br /> <br /> Gunzosha armour is still a thing, and we'll be getting a write-up for it soon with supplementary Dragon Blooded material, so that handily resolves the question of whether or not there's an eye to regular people being able to access the benefits of these things.<br /> <br /> And even without all of that, what you're saying there does not match the overall setting tone; in addition to the sorcerous workings that people have already mentioned, there are a number of hearthstones that have been written up that project beneficial effects over an area, that can be used to improve general life. I can't say what manses will do yet, since they're one thing that we haven't really gotten anything for, but I'd say there's a good basis for expecting some things that have similar uses.<br /> <br /> (There's an inherent bias there against the value of farming, but it's not the subject of the thread, so I'll say nothing about it besides it being irrelevant to my assessment of what the game enables somebody to provide)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T08:10:46-07:00","id":1244495,"title":"","content":"Plus, a large-scale transport system is one of the biggest ways to directly improve the overall quality of life for entire regions. IE.<br /> <br /> Step 1: Build an artifact train system<br /> Step 2:<br /> Step 3: Everyone profits.<br /> <br /> Just because you can't mass produce <i>storied magical weapons and armor</i> doesn't mean you can't fantastically improve the lives of countless millions of people.<br /> <br /> I'll also point out that there is nothing stopping you from mass producing mundane weapons. The only thing this prevents is equipping an army of mortals with bland, samey magical arms and armor which <i>they can't even use anyway!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 08-10-2018, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T09:10:39-07:00","id":1244832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1244264#post1244264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e's insistence that you can't mass-produce artifacts in any shape or way whatsoever</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, strange, in my copy of Arms of the Chosen, on p.125, it says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> MYRIAD MANUFACTURE<br /> While marvels such as daiklaves or warstriders are always unique (p. 12), some artifacts, such as Brass Legionnaires, exist as part of a greater whole. In the First Age, Creation-wide webs of miraculous infrastructure permitted artificers to manufacture such artifacts in batches. Without that infrastructure, creating artifacts on such a scale is impossible. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T16:42:01-07:00","id":1244969,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:8px\">it's almost like most people complaining about 3e craft haven't even read it.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T16:51:38-07:00","id":1244972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1244969#post1244969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">it's almost like most people complaining about 3e craft haven't even read it.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, most people who complain about it have definitely read it in detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T05:19:03-07:00","id":1245089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rj.au</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1244419#post1244419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give them to martially inclined gods to win their favour. Supply them to outcaste terrestrial families to incentivise them to stay on your good side. Give them to NPC celestial exalted in exchange for their help. Give them to desperate dynasts willing to bargain with anathemas in the hope of defeating their rivals. Give them to abyssals in exchange for eclipse-sanctified vows not to attack your subjects. Use a different one each story then sell them to collectors of historically important weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still not going to be most people's definition of churning out daiklaves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T05:36:07-07:00","id":1245090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1244969#post1244969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">it's almost like most people complaining about 3e craft haven't even read it.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Arms of the chosen is a seperate supplement that not many people have access too. It doesn't alter the crafting part of the solar charmset. It does change the evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T06:00:07-07:00","id":1245094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1245089#post1245089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's still not going to be most people's definition of churning out daiklaves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, one daiklaive a story isn't that quick. One artefact a story seems like a reasonable rate for someone who's sunk a fair bit of XP into Craft, tbh. And it's pretty achievable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T06:04:55-07:00","id":1245096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1245090#post1245090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arms of the chosen is a seperate supplement that not many people have access too.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing that on?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does change the evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. They actually dropped an idea that the prior developers had for changing Evocations, and stuck to the solid course established by the core.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T08:04:47-07:00","id":1245112,"title":"","content":"Artifacts created to be used as bargaining chips should probably made specifically for whoever you are bargaining with. <br /> <br /> Not &quot;Oh, I need to butter up this guy&quot; *rummages around massive pile of daiklaves* &quot;yeah, I think he'll like this one&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T10:33:19-07:00","id":1245139,"title":"","content":"The idea that a Solar can by herself crank out a lot of daiklaves like some crazy swordsmith is not in itself soemthing 3e is against.<br /> <br /> What it is more against, in my understanding, is stuff like having a Factory-Cathedral pump out a battlegroup's worth of daiklaves in the span it took to build a singl eone, with each one bieng identical and not having anything ot them save being made out of fancy alloyed steel. The former is an extension of the fact that you make a lot of daiklaves, and the result is something that is sitlle ach a unique piece of artifice by the builder. The other is industrialization of osmething not really meant to be industrialized for setting coherency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T11:02:08-07:00","id":1245142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1245139#post1245139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that a Solar can by herself crank out a lot of daiklaves like some crazy swordsmith is not in itself soemthing 3e is against.<br /> <br /> What it is more against, in my understanding, is stuff like having a Factory-Cathedral pump out a battlegroup's worth of daiklaves in the span it took to build a singl eone, with each one bieng identical and not having anything ot them save being made out of fancy alloyed steel. The former is an extension of the fact that you make a lot of daiklaves, and the result is something that is sitlle ach a unique piece of artifice by the builder. The other is industrialization of osmething not really meant to be industrialized for setting coherency.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my understanding too, it\u2019s the idea of wholesale mass production of artifacts, or to put it another the industrialization of artifacts without the use of first age artifice, that 3e is not a fan of. That\u2019s not to say you can\u2019t make a shining wonderous city on the hill, but that should be something a solar is building toward throughout an entire chronicle. It\u2019s why there is an emphasis on sorcerous workings, to show what had to be in place for that wonderous infrastructure to work. What i think 3e is against is the genericization of artifacts into magic sword+1. Just my two cents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T11:04:40-07:00","id":1245143,"title":"","content":"If you make a lot of daiklaves at once they should be part of a set and do shit when you get all of them together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T11:59:41-07:00","id":1245151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1245143#post1245143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you make a lot of daiklaves at once they should be part of a set and do shit when you get all of them together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm down for that too! It's why I actually mentioned the anime/light novel <b>Katanagatari</b>. One of the 13 evil swords in that series is...actually a set of like 100 swords that are all <i>actually</i> the same sword. Shit like that's cool, but it should be done so you actually are taking their large amount into account for the story, rather than just trying to outfit folks with marginally better-statted weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T15:49:41-07:00","id":1245217,"title":"","content":"Paired blades like Courant and Galliard, the twin blades of Razor Dancer and Wise Steel or the twin Devil Casters suggested with Sirrush, or a set of five blades made specifically for a Circle, Fellowship, or Brotherhood, etc. Awesome.<br /> <br /> &quot;I pumped out so many daiklaves today I didn't even bother naming them all&quot;: Meh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T15:58:22-07:00","id":1245220,"title":"","content":"&quot;After mechanically churning out hundreds of daiklaves in the course of several weeks, I finally created my magnum opus: Gudsord, the Generic Blade. A sword so utterly mundane it cannot be described&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T21:16:00-07:00","id":1245316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1241090-artifact-costs?p=1245220#post1245220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;After mechanically churning out hundreds of daiklaves in the course of several weeks, I finally created my magnum opus: Gudsord, the Generic Blade. A sword so utterly mundane it cannot be described&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, possible origin story of the forgotten blade?<br /> <br /> Just kidding, onto more serious ideas:<br /> I would love a quest for a matching set of artifacts that complement each other and harmonize well together. One for each good guy PC, and maybe wearable all by one person as the evil collector.<br /> <br /> So maybe: armor, sword, smashfist/shield, bow, and like a helmet or crown. Each a different color of jade, buffed evocations when 'near' another of the set.<br /> <br /> The problem ive had with mass artifact creation concerning weapons like daiklaves that i feel 3rd edition adresses better in mechanics but leaves vague on fluff is that, translated to D&amp;D, Daiklaves are already the +5 flaming vicious vorpal swords. At 3 dots. 4 and 5 dots add nothing mathwise to your stats, they just expand your evocation options. D&amp;D having plain +1 and +2 swords was strange but understandable for its math side of the game. Exalted, especially 3rd, doesn't really run like that. And the combat abilities (for solars at least) can let you skip needing an artifact at all and just summon your weapon out of light, even with evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}